### W1: the start-up refusal of a malformed FollowUp value (create; Task; priority Low; labels `rec-2026-11-16`, `follow-up`; marker `REC-LND3-16NOV-W1`)
SUMMARY-W1: Start-up now reads the FollowUp options: a malformed FollowUp value (for example FollowUp:SessionMinutes=abc) stops the host from starting, where before pull request 328 the host started and only follow-up requests failed; accepted as built

BEGIN BODY-W1
BLUF: Pull request 328 (the start-up warning for FollowUp:TrustedProxies, merged to main 2026-11-16, not deployed) reads the follow-up options when the host starts. A malformed FollowUp value, for example FollowUp:SessionMinutes=abc, now stops the host from starting with the binder's error, "Failed to convert configuration value 'abc' at 'FollowUp:SessionMinutes'". At main before the change (3e557e56) the host started and only the follow-up requests would have failed. The settings that ship, and valid values, are unaffected.
Recommendation: Keep it as built: a bad configuration value is found when the host is deployed and started, not later as broken follow-up requests. The effect was accepted as a design choice inside the commissioned work by the person directing that work; it is not a ruling of the product owner and no card was ruled. Proposed default if nobody objects: no change. If the earlier behaviour (start, and fail only the follow-up requests) is wanted, that is a code change and its own decision.
Detail: From the independent review of pull request 328 (its finding 1, Major in the review's own words, "claim contradicted; not a blocker"). The builder's commit message said "no behaviour change"; the review measured otherwise with a probe: with FollowUp:SessionMinutes=abc the host fails to start at head, and the same test with main's Program.cs passes. The line that does it resolves the follow-up options at start-up (api/src/HpsmPoc.Api/Program.cs:133 at main <<MAIN8>>). The change's own squash text says so: "The follow-up options are now read at start-up, so a malformed FollowUp value" and "stops the host at start-up instead of failing the follow-up requests later;". Not measured: which other FollowUp settings can fail to bind (the review probed one); whether any hosted setting holds a malformed FollowUp value (no host was read for this ticket).
Done when: the effect is recorded as accepted as built, or a change that keeps the earlier behaviour is made.
Records: entry C-<<CE1>> in the project's clarifications record.
Marker: [REC-LND3-16NOV-W1]
END BODY-W1

